1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,045
PRAMAAN, which means proof.

2
00:00:02,045 --> 00:00:11,813
Face liveness and presentation attack detection for the MOSIP Registration Client, for MOSIP Decode 2026, problem statement four.

3
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:19,006
One honest note first: this is a working engine that has not yet been measured on real attacks.

4
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:21,501
The preview is unsigned.

5
00:00:21,501 --> 00:00:24,261
The capture that is stored is signed.

6
00:00:24,261 --> 00:00:25,903
Nothing links the two.

7
00:00:25,903 --> 00:00:32,991
So whoever controls the preview can pass liveness with one face while another face is enrolled.

8
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:36,796
On Android, the client never even sees the preview.

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:51,822
PRAMAAN defines the two interfaces the problem statement asks for: a frame source that returns frames and the signed capture from the same object, and a liveness engine that takes frames in and gives states, guidance and a decision out.

10
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:58,844
The next screens are the real station user interface, driven by a simulated session.

11
00:00:58,844 --> 00:01:01,328
No camera or device is connected.

12
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:04,947
The operator signs in with their face.

13
00:01:04,947 --> 00:01:10,933
If the framing is poor, the screen gives guidance, such as please move closer.

14
00:01:10,933 --> 00:01:13,543
It is never reported as an attack.

15
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:18,857
For the resident, the operator can tick accessibility needs.

16
00:01:18,857 --> 00:01:21,166
The system chooses the checks.

17
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:24,013
The resident never picks a challenge.

18
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:34,523
If the passive checks are not enough, the engine asks for something a recording cannot contain, chosen at random, with an icon and a spoken prompt.

19
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:38,414
When the action is detected, the screen says so.

20
00:01:38,414 --> 00:01:46,332
There is no score and no progress bar, because the number of steps must not tell the resident how the system sees them.

21
00:01:47,030 --> 00:01:54,358
On success, the packet is written with signed liveness evidence, so a server can re-check the decision later.

22
00:01:55,060 --> 00:02:05,045
When an attempt fails, the resident sees one generic sentence, the attempt number, and a wait that depends only on how many attempts were used.

23
00:02:05,045 --> 00:02:06,233
Never on a score.

24
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:17,443
If a resident cannot pass, a supervisor, not the operator, approves an exception with a reason, by passing their own fresh liveness check.

25
00:02:17,443 --> 00:02:19,043
That is dual control.

26
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:24,316
Finally, a supervisor approves the packet with their own face.

27
00:02:24,316 --> 00:02:27,638
The operator cannot approve their own packet.

28
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:32,291
Every screen is also in Hindi, switched with one click.

29
00:02:32,291 --> 00:02:37,463
The Hindi was drafted by machine and verified by a native Hindi speaker.

30
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,629
And it fails closed.

31
00:02:39,629 --> 00:02:48,443
If the policy, a model or the certificate does not verify, nothing can be registered, and the screen says what to check.

32
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,956
Now the capture binding.

33
00:02:50,956 --> 00:03:02,533
Four locks run before any accept: the session nonce echoed inside the device signed capture, a hash chain over the frames, identity continuity, and time.

34
00:03:02,533 --> 00:03:05,862
Each attack is a test, and each is rejected.

35
00:03:05,862 --> 00:03:08,662
These locks work on unmodified S B I.

36
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:11,414
We also attacked ourselves.

37
00:03:11,414 --> 00:03:13,164
This is synthetic data.

38
00:03:13,164 --> 00:03:21,839
With the passive model assumed fooled and no flash light, the fusion accepted four of eighty five display pitches.

39
00:03:21,839 --> 00:03:23,741
With the flash cue, none.

40
00:03:23,741 --> 00:03:28,002
We logged it and fixed it for operators and supervisors.

41
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:31,751
What we verify, and what we do not claim.

42
00:03:31,751 --> 00:03:35,324
Seven hundred thirty eight automated tests pass.

43
00:03:35,324 --> 00:03:41,427
We have not measured an error rate on real attacks, because no real corpus exists.

44
00:03:41,427 --> 00:03:47,902
The models and camera were timed on one phone, but no full session has run on a device.

45
00:03:47,902 --> 00:03:54,600
The moire cue, measured on one camera, does not separate live from replay, so it abstains.

46
00:03:55,300 --> 00:04:02,497
Patches for the desktop and Android Registration Clients apply cleanly to MOSIP's code.

47
00:04:02,497 --> 00:04:04,317
Android is hooks only.

48
00:04:04,317 --> 00:04:09,694
Next: one real experiment, a consented corpus, and a real device.

49
00:04:09,694 --> 00:04:15,401
We would like to ask MOSIP how an S B I extension should be proposed.

50
00:04:15,401 --> 00:04:19,124
The code is M P L two point zero, like MOSIP.

51
00:04:19,124 --> 00:04:19,951
Thank you.

